     ggrroouuppmmoodd — modify an existing group on the system

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ggrroouuppmmoodd [--oovv] [--gg _g_i_d] [--nn _n_e_w_n_a_m_e] _g_r_o_u_p

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggrroouuppmmoodd utility modifies an existing group.  The options are as fol‐
     lows:

     --gg _g_i_d  Gives the numeric group identifier to be used for the new group.

     --nn _n_e_w_n_a_m_e
             Gives the new name which the group shall have.

     --oo      Allows the new group to have a GID which is already in use for
             another group.

     --vv      Enables verbose mode - explain the commands as they are executed.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ggrroouuppmmoodd utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

